[Music]  hello my friends i hope you're all doing  well i wanted to give a few updates  regarding my plans for the channel in  2022 and beyond i could have done this  in a community post i guess but aside  from potentially typing out a whole  dictionary i also think that actually  talking to you guys like this is a more  real and effective way to get my  thoughts out you know emotional process  and all so there's a couple of things to  mention and i'll start with the main  topic and then cover some additional  stuff after that if you've been  following my twitter or maybe some of my  live streams you may have caught on to  the fact that i am very excited for from  software's upcoming title elden ring  it's a game that similar to breath of  the wild has been in development for  quite a long time in fact it was first  announced in 2019 at the same e3 as  breath 202's reveal and well as you  probably have guessed from the thumbnail  alone i'm planning to make content about  eldon ring i think it's a game that fits  the channel really well i mean it's an  open world medieval fantasy game where  you explore vast landscapes filled with  ancient ruins tons of challenging  enemies and bosses and dungeons hidden  throughout the world waiting to be  discovered and from what we've been able  to see so far it's also packed to the  brim with story and lore to those of you  who are only here for the zelda content  i want to put your mind at ease by  saying zelda videos are not going  anywhere it is and always will be a main  focus of this channel and i still have  plenty of ideas for future videos  including a follow-up to life as a  bokoblin later this year i'll make sure  to balance it out so you're not just  getting alden ring stuff for weeks upon  end zelda is the foundation upon which  monster maze was built so disregarding  that would be foolish that being said i  have been looking for an opportunity to  branch out just a little bit more after  all zelda games take a long time to make  it's why this series is so good but that  also means that sometimes there's a lot  less to talk about and i want to avoid  reaching for subjects and forcing out  content just to please the algorithm  having something on the side can  definitely help with that if i have  inspiration for a zelda video i will  make one if i don't or if i feel like  the idea needs more time to develop i  can focus on something else for a bit of  course i'm not expecting any of you to  watch my elden ring content just for the  sake of supporting me not everyone is  going to be interested in it or has the  means to play it so that would be a very  unrealistic expectation but who knows  maybe my videos will sway some of you to  give the game a try and join me in  exploring this world and unraveling its  story and mysteries i have some more to  say about breathtak 2 in particular but  i'll save that for the very end to avoid  rambling too much and you know get  through the announcements first some of  you may have noticed that my upload  schedule hasn't been as consistent as it  was say a year ago when i was cranking  out at least one video every weekend  like clockwork i can assure you that  it's not because i've gotten lazy or  because i lost my motivation in any way  it's got more to do with the fact that  i've come to value the quality of my  productions above anything else and i  want to continue to improve my skills as  an editor animator storyteller etc even  when i try to make something simple  nowadays i still end up going the extra  mile regardless i can't seem to switch  it off my latest video about the spider  houses for example was supposed to be  just a quick 10 minute video without too  much effort put into it since i just got  done making those breath 202 patent  videos i figured i should probably give  myself a break and well lo and behold it  still ended up becoming a 20 minute  video the script kept on growing and  growing which also meant having to  capture more and more footage not to  mention that my capture card crashed  halfway without me knowing so about half  of the footage came back as a black  screen so i had to recapture all of it  which ended up delaying the video and by  that point i was like well i might as  well animate some cool looking title  cards now too i gotta have nice looking  title cards making animations no matter  how simple is and always will be one of  my biggest passions and i know myself  well enough to know that i don't have  the type of brain that can just keep  doing the same thing over and over again  eventually i will get sick of it if i do  challenging myself as much as possible  and trying out new things for every  video will ensure that i'll continue to  find enjoyment in making them for many  years to come even if that means i  cannot produce videos as fast as i used  to that doesn't mean i'm going to keep  you guys waiting for months in between  videos and it's only going to get worse  over time i'm definitely planning to  keep the content flowing at a reasonable  pace all i'm saying is don't always  expect a video every week sometimes you  might have to wait two maybe even three  weeks depending on the scale of the  project i'm working on which ties into  the next subject i've been wanting to  try out a podcast type of format on the  channel for a while now and i think it's  about time i get started on that in the  time spent as a creator i've been able  to get acquainted with a lot of amazing  people and i feel like it would be a lot  of fun to sit down with them for an hour  or so and just talk about stuff this  includes fellow zelda theorists other  creators i admire or look up to real  life friends people in the gaming  industry anyone i can convince to share  a bit of their time with me really of  course oftentimes zelda will be a big  focus of the conversations but i will  definitely allow the subject matter to  go into completely different directions  too it kind of depends on the type of  guest i have on if it's a speedrunner  it's going to be more about speedrunning  if it's a modder or a voice actor i'm  definitely going to want to pick their  brains on their speciality doing a  podcast will also allow me to fill in  potential gaps in between bigger  projects since they are much less labor  intensive i'm still working out the  details on when exactly i want to  kickstart the podcast and what the  upload schedule will be it's probably  not going to be a weekly thing because i  don't want to run out of guests too  quickly and you know people are also  busy so it's nice if they have at least  a two week notice so i'm guessing  probably once every two weeks but we'll  see how it turns out next is streaming  not too long ago i kind of sort of made  a deal with my audience that i would  stream every week on the same day  wednesday to be exact and i managed to  keep that consistent for barely three  weeks until i already started to falter  i gotta say true to myself i'm just not  that much of a streamer at least not on  a schedule i enjoy doing the nintendo  direct streams and those will definitely  remain a tradition and every once in a  while i do find it enjoyable to  spontaneously kickstart a zelda stream  and just roll with it but a weekly  streaming schedule is just not gonna  work for me a lot of the time i'd rather  work on a video and having to stream on  a set day often gets in the way not only  that but despite being a general  optimist i am very mood sensitive i have  this thing called panic anxiety disorder  and while it's not a huge issue in my  life by any means it does sometimes  creep up on me at random and when it  does i don't really want to interact  with people and much prefer to just be  on my own so there you go a little  private detail about me again not saying  i won't do regular streams anymore  altogether but just treat it like the  spanish inquisition don't expect it all  in all i think we're in for a very good  year and aside from elden ring i might  even cover more franchises and subjects  in the future xenoblade chronicles 3  comes to mind i'm very much invested in  the story of the xenoblade universe so  i'm definitely considering making videos  about that too as we get closer to the  release of that game i want to emphasize  that even though i'm branching out a bit  more that doesn't mean that my hype and  interest for breathtak 2 or the series  as a whole for that matter is dwindling  not even close i know some of you are  disappointed that breath 202 hasn't  shown up again in the last few months  and i totally get that first the game  awards and now the february direct it  was a bit of a double whammy but as i  stated before good games take time not  to mention we just had a global pandemic  to deal with if anything the game's  prolonged absence likely means that they  are taking their time and when nintendo  takes their time it's bound to be really  freaking good i also think they want to  avoid some of the mistakes they made  with the development cycle of the  original breath of the wild as some of  you may remember they weren't exactly  proficient with the promotion of that  game especially in the beginning first  it was going to be 2015 then 2016 then  it ended up becoming a switch title it's  clear that they were sort of winging it  i'm guessing they realize that not  making too many promises is better than  making promises you cannot keep i mean  just look at how it ended up for  cyberpunk a lot of promises and  mechanics that never even made it in i'm  confident that when nintendo is finally  ready to go all out with the game's  promotion it'll be amazing and the  release won't be too far off anyway my  voice is already starting to wear down  so that's enough rambling for one video  i thank you all for your time your  support ideas feedback and all that good  jazz i hope you look forward to my  upcoming videos bye

